<LockabularyPage title="Lockabulary privacy policy" description="Lockabulary collects no data. Progress stays on your devices and in your private iCloud." path="lockabulary/privacy">
  <h1>Lockabulary privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="soft">Last updated 26 October 2026</p>

  <p>Lockabulary is a vocabulary trainer for iPhone and Mac made by Artur Witkowski. It has no account, no ads, no analytics and no server. I don't collect any data about you.</p>

  <h2>What stays on your devices</h2>
  <p>Your words, answers, progress and settings are saved on your iPhone and Mac. If you're signed in to iCloud, Lockabulary syncs them between your devices through your private iCloud database. Apple stores that database under your Apple Account, and I can't read it.</p>

  <h2>Screen Time</h2>
  <p>On iPhone, Lockabulary uses Apple's Screen Time framework to lock the apps you choose. iOS hands the app only opaque tokens for those apps, so Lockabulary never learns which apps or websites they are. It counts minutes of use on the device to know when to lock, and that count never leaves the device.</p>

  <h2>Bug reports and ideas</h2>
  <p>"Report a bug" and "Suggest an idea" open an email in your own mail app, addressed to contact@arturwitkowski.com. A bug report includes the app's log of what it did and when, plus your app version, system version, device model and the language you're learning. You see all of it before you send, and nothing goes anywhere unless you press send. I use these emails only to answer you and fix the app.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Lockabulary collects no data from anyone, children included. On a child's account in Family Sharing, a parent approves Screen Time access.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>Delete the app to remove its data from a device. To remove the iCloud copy, open Settings, tap your name, then iCloud, and manage storage for Lockabulary.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be on this page with a new date. Questions go to <a href="mailto:contact@arturwitkowski.com">contact@arturwitkowski.com</a>.</p>
</LockabularyPage>
